---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { publishedGoals } from '../lib/goals';
import { credits } from '../lib/images';
// site-imagery §1: one line per image a page shows, written from the manifest; no image in use, no section.
const photoCredits = credits(publishedGoals());
---
<Base title="About — Cut the Ties" description="Who runs Cut the Ties and how it is paid for.">
  <section class="mx-auto px-4 lg:px-10 py-10 max-w-2xl">
    <h1 class="display-lg">About</h1>
    <div class="prose-cut mt-6">
      <p>Cut the Ties is built and run by one volunteer. It is not a PAC, a campaign or an organisation, and it is not affiliated with any candidate or party.</p>
      <h2>What it does</h2>
      <p>You enter your address. The site finds your House district and senators and shows the two open decisions where a call from you matters most this week, then helps you write the call script or letter. Every vote count, position and date comes from a sourced row in the project's public data files, not from a language model.</p>
      <h2>Who pays</h2>
      <p>The site is paid for out of pocket and by <a href="/donate">donations</a>. Donations are not tax-deductible and are not political contributions to any candidate.</p>
      <h2>Your data</h2>
      <p>What is stored, and what is sent where, is on the <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>.</p>
      {photoCredits.length > 0 && (
        <Fragment>
          <h2 id="photo-credits">Photo credits</h2>
          <ul>
            {photoCredits.map((c) => (
              <li data-credit={c.id}>{c.generated ? c.text : <Fragment>{c.alt}: {c.author}, <a href={c.source_url} rel="noopener">{c.source}</a> ({c.licence_label})</Fragment>}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </Fragment>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
